  "name": "Assiko (Bassa guitar-and-bottle dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dance music of the Bassa of the Littoral and Centre regions of Cameroon, in which a singer is accompanied by a guitar and by a percussionist striking an empty bottle with metal knives and forks. Jean Bikoko 'Aladin', whose singles of the 1960s and 1970s made the style widely known, is regarded as its leading exponent. The bottle-percussion card stands in for the struck bottle.",
